## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design scalable, tenant-aware ML pipelines with calibration, streaming features, drift handling, and safe rollout strategies across enterprise-scale tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant feature stores and leakage prevention
- Shared base model + per-tenant calibrator
- Real-time features from streaming usage and billing
- Online retraining with drift detectors
- Offline + online evaluation and staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo calibration hook
function calibrate(probs, tenantId, store){
  const params = store.getParams(tenantId)
  // adjust by temp scaler
  return Math.min(0.999, Math.max(0.001, probs * params.scale + params.bias))
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant calibration offline and online?
- How would you guard against cross-tenant data leakage in CV and feature drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a production-ready online continual learning system under delayed feedback, latency, memory limits, and non-stationary user behavior, with fairness concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Online continual learning with delayed labels
- Factorization machines and warm-start online SGD
- Calibration, drift detection, and memory-budget governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton online update loop for streaming features
function onlineUpdate(x, y, w, lr) {
  const pred = 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-dot(w, x)));
  const g = pred - y;
  for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) w[i] -= lr * g * x[i];
  return w;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor for calibration drift in production?
- How would you enforce fairness constraints without sacrificing overall performance?

